# the object's debug records as DWARF 5 debugging information
#
# one compile unit holds the records, written into .debug_info,
# .debug_abbrev, .debug_addr, .debug_loclists and .debug_rnglists, or the
# names the format's row gives them, in DWARF 5 forms throughout: a string in
# place (DW_FORM_string), an address by its index into the address table
# (DW_FORM_addrx), and a location or range list by its index
# (DW_FORM_loclistx, DW_FORM_rnglistx). a list over code of fixed size
# states each range by its offsets from a base address, a location list's
# from its function's start (DW_LLE_base_addressx, DW_LLE_offset_pair) and a
# range list's by its start and length (DW_RLE_startx_length). over code the
# linker may resize, a location list states each range by its two addresses
# (DW_LLE_start_end) and a range list by two indexes (DW_RLE_startx_endx).
# a variable in one place over all of its function's code is located by an
# expression alone. every address is a datum of the address width relocated
# against the mark or symbol it names, and every reference between the
# sections an offset relocated by the section-relative kind against the start
# of the section it names. an address and a list each take the next index the
# first time an entry names it, in the order the entries are written.
#
# the unit's entry comes first, then each global, then the abstract entry of
# every callee inlined, then each function with its variables and the code
# inlined in it, with no children for a function of neither, then each type
# the entries name, and each type those name, until every type named is
# written. a type names another by its entry's offset, filled once every type
# is written. a structure, union, tagged union or enumeration with a key is
# described once in a program: the object it is the own type of writes it as a
# type unit after the compile unit in the same section, one another object
# describes is a declaration naming that unit's signature (DW_AT_signature),
# and a shared one, which every object naming it describes alike, is a type
# unit of its own in a section of its own, in a group whose signature is the
# unit's, where the format's links keep one copy of a group of sections by its
# signature, and is written in each unit that names it elsewhere. every unit
# that names a type unit other than its own holds a declaration of it naming
# its signature, which is the hash of the type's key alone, so every object
# names it alike without describing it. a tagged union is a structure of its discriminant and a variant
# part of its cases. a variable's location list has an entry per range where
# DWARF can state where it is, so a debugger reads it as optimised out
# elsewhere: a
# frame slot or a webassembly location with steps over it is one DWARF's
# expressions do not state. a global of the unit is at its symbol's address,
# a thread-local at its symbol's offset in its thread's block before
# DW_OP_form_tls_address in the form the format's row states, with no
# location where the object's relocations write none of the row's kinds, and
# one another unit defines is a declaration. a declaration's file and line,
# and the unit's DW_AT_stmt_list, are written where the object's line records
# lowered to a DWARF line table, its file k the line table's file k. the
# encoding is 32-bit DWARF.

use std.types.bool.bool;
use std.types.bool.false;
use std.types.bool.true;
use std.types.error.err;
use std.types.option.opt;
use std.types.result.res;
